{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_82","type":"agent_message","text":"# Implementation Notes\n\n## Decisions Made\n- Added `TankState::avg_substrate_index(...)` as the shared depth-weighted, clamped helper and used it for detritus trapping, shrimp grazing access, and periphyton carrying capacity.\n- Wired filter hardware into nitrification and DO causally: `filter.enabled` now penalizes nitrifier environment when off, `flow_lph` scales nitrifier vmax when on, and running filter flow adds a small `k_la` boost.\n- Added daily filter clogging progression in the daily update path, gated on `filter.enabled`, with invariant-safe clamping on `clogging_index`.\n- Added a hidden `daily_food_consumed_g` shrimp state field so grazing-surface changes affect actual shrimp condition instead of only depleting food pools; tuned the condition mapping to preserve existing reproduction/regression behavior.\n\n## Spec Deviations\n- Used the acceptance-criteria clogging formula as the source of truth. `clogging_index` increases only by `0.002 * (1.0 - cleanliness_index) * detritus_pressure` when the filter is enabled, without extra `flow_lph` scaling beyond the prose description, because the acceptance criteria specified an exact increment expression.\n- No other deviations.\n\n## Testing\n- Added the four required integration tests: `substrate_trapping_divergence`, `substrate_grazing_divergence`, `filter_enabled_vs_disabled`, and `filter_flow_affects_cycling`.\n- Verified the full workspace with:\n  - `nix shell nixpkgs#cargo nixpkgs#rustc nixpkgs#rustfmt nixpkgs#gcc -c cargo test`\n\n---"}}
